  "_comment": [
    "TV Thing's channel lineup, laid out like an old cable lineup card (lineup.py reads it).",
    "A channel is its source and its id there: an antenna channel by its virtual number (digital 22.4),",
    "a Roku feed by its YouTube TV row (youtube-tv NBC). 'name' renames it in the lineup; 'note' is for",
    "people reading this file and is ignored. Games sections number each day's games by kickoff; the two",
    "Live Sports games sections are one block, football, baseball and hockey together, split around",
    "VizelVision on 70. 60 heads Live Sports with VizelVision's Sports Guide, today's games as slides",
    "(source vizelvision with a channel: one of the station's slide channels). A channel not listed here takes the",
    "first free number in the section whose 'new' names its source ('*' = any other), and keeps it in",
    "lineup_state.json; list it here to move it. 22-28 are held for a Lansing / Flint antenna receiver;",
    "29 is Pentulive, an internet stream (internet_streams.json)."
